# Config file folding

This file anchors VS Code's file-nesting rules: the repo's root-level config
files nest under it in the explorer, and the `$` sorts it above the source
directories. To enable, add the following to your VS Code settings.json and
adjust the list to your own config surface:

```jsonc
"explorer.fileNesting.enabled": true,
"explorer.fileNesting.patterns": {
  "package.json": "-package-lock.json, yarn.lock, pnpm-lock.yaml, bun.lockb, bun.lock",
  // - VS Code nests lockfiles under package.json by default. Prefix with '-' so
  //    package-lock.json nests under $config instead.
  "$config": ".editorconfig, .gitattributes, .gitignore, deno.json, deno.jsonc, deno.lock, package.json, package-lock.json, tsconfig.*"
},
```
